    "content": "Yes, the Johnson Space Center (JSC) in Houston, Texas, is highly active and serves as the hub for human spaceflight operations. As of April 2026, it is actively directing the Artemis II lunar mission, managing International Space Station (ISS) operations, and training astronauts. Key, active roles include: Mission Control Center: Provides real-time, 24/7 operational support for ISS and crewed missions. Astronaut Training: Home to the U.S. astronaut corps and training facilities like the Neutral Buoyancy Laboratory. Artemis Program: Leads the development of the Orion spacecraft and Gateway lunar outpost. Commercial Crew: Collaborates with private firms, such as Axiom Space, for missions to the ISS. The site also houses the Space Center Houston, which serves as the public visitor center. Space Center Houston",
